{"content":[{"c":["MARESHAH (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City (Greek ",{"c":["Marisa"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"},{"c":[";"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," Josephus, “Marissa”) on the road from the coastal plain of Judah toward Hebron and Jerusalem. Remains of Jewish pottery indicate occupation from at least 800 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". The site is now called Tel Mareshah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["At Israel’s occupation of Canaan, Mareshah was allotted by Joshua to Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.44","r":"Josh.15.44","rawR":"Josh.15.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.44","value":"Josh.15.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:44"},"). Later, at the division of the kingdom, Rehoboam fortified it as a protective outpost covering Jerusalem from the southwest, from which many invaders were to approach (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.8","r":"2Chr.11.8","rawR":"2Chr.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.8","value":"2Chr.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:8"},"). Zerah the Ethiopian, with a million men and three hundred chariots, penetrated as far as Mareshah and was defeated there by Asa (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.14.9","r":"2Chr.14.9","rawR":"2Chr.14.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.14.9","value":"2Chr.14.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:9"},"). In the following reign, that of Jehoshaphat, the prophet Eliezer, born at Mareshah, foretold the destruction of the proud fleet the king had built (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.37","r":"2Chr.20.37","rawR":"2Chr.20.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.37","value":"2Chr.20.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:37"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The prophet Micah, who was born at Moresheth-gath (a few miles to the north), uttered a moving elegy upon the fate of the regions he knew from boyhood, as the Assyrians approached (whether under Sennacherib, 701 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", or Sargon, 711 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). Punning upon each familiar place-name, he warned Mareshah of a coming “possessor” (",{"href":"?bref=Mic.1.15","r":"Mic.1.15","rawR":"Mic.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.1.15","value":"Mic.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 1:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MareshahPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.44","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.44","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.44"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.8","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.8","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.8"},{"anchorText":"14:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.14.9","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.14.9","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.14.9"},{"anchorText":"20:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.20.37","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.20.37","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.20.37"},{"anchorText":"Mi 1:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.1.15","rawQueryValue":"Mic.1.15","sourceRefExact":"Mic.1.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2d33cdb4b4ae6554a5408ffd49369e990367bcafbc06839bc403d3793f278acc","sourceItemName":"MareshahPlace","sourceItemOrder":138,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"AerialViewOfTellMareshah","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MareshahPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mareshah (Place)","title":"Mareshah (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}